  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is linked to SQ20B through a series of molecular interactions involving the P2X purinoceptor 1 and [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate. This compound is identified as a target of Mollicellin N, and it in turn targets SQ20B. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N acts as a modulator of the P2X purinoceptor 1, which is a key receptor in cellular signaling pathways. The presence of multiple paths with similar scores indicates a consistent and robust relationship between Mollicellin N and SQ20B, likely through the intermediate of the P2X purinoceptor 1. The mechanism appears to involve a direct or indirect interaction where Mollicellin N influences the activity of the P2X receptor, which then affects the target SQ20B. This pathway highlights the role of the P2X purinoceptor in mediating the effects of Mollicellin N on SQ20B, suggesting a potential therapeutic or pharmacological significance.",
